## 📌 **Detailed Project Roadmap & Feature Backlog**

Below is the complete roadmap with clearly defined features and tasks from start to finish, optimized for an AI agent to execute step-by-step.

### 📌 **Phase 1: Project Initialization & Setup**
- [ ] Initialize Git Repository & README documentation
- [ ] Set up Docker and Docker-compose environments
- [ ] Define project directory structure (frontend/backend)
- [ ] Configure `.env` file for sensitive keys & credentials

### 📌 **Phase 2: Backend (FastAPI) Core Setup**
- [ ] Create FastAPI boilerplate (`main.py`, `routes.py`)
- [ ] Install dependencies (`FastAPI`, `Uvicorn`, `Pydantic`, `HTTPX`, `python-dotenv`)
- [ ] Setup basic healthcheck endpoint (`/ping`)

### 📌 **Phase 3: Frontend (React) Setup**
- [ ] Initialize React with Vite and TypeScript
- [ ] Install core libraries (`Axios`, `React Router DOM`, `TailwindCSS`, `ShadCN UI`)
- [ ] Create basic app structure (`App.tsx`, `Home.tsx`, component folders)

### 📌 **Phase 4: AI & LLM Layer Integration**
- [ ] Integrate OpenAI API SDK (`openai-python`)
- [ ] Integrate Ollama API for local models
- [ ] Setup agent runner logic (`agent_runner.py`) to manage model calls

### 📌 **Phase 5: Embeddings & Context Management**
- [ ] Set up embeddings storage (ChromaDB/FAISS)
- [ ] Create Context & Memory APIs for managing custom contexts
- [ ] Develop a schema for dynamic agent-generated data storage and retrieval

### 📌 **Phase 6: Workflow Automation Engine**
- [ ] Integrate N8N workflow builder
- [ ] Develop API to interface workflows with FastAPI backend
- [ ] Allow agent-driven creation and execution of automated workflows

### 📌 **Phase 7: Custom Dashboard & Visualization**
- [ ] Integrate React Grid Layout for dashboard builder
- [ ] Use Recharts or Chart.js for visual data representation
- [ ] Develop frontend API connectors for real-time and historical data visualization

### 📌 **Phase 8: Agent Terminal & Output Viewer**
- [ ] Develop a UI to interact directly with agents (send prompts, receive outputs)
- [ ] Create real-time log output and status viewer via WebSockets/Socket.IO
- [ ] Implement dynamic interaction history (user-agent conversation context)

### 📌 **Phase 9: Scheduler & Automation**
- [ ] Set up scheduler (`scheduler.py`) for automated agent tasks
- [ ] Implement task queuing system with Redis or FastAPI background tasks
- [ ] Develop APIs to define scheduled and repeating workflows

### 📌 **Phase 10: External Data Integrations**
- [ ] Integrate financial data APIs (Polygon.io, Alpha Vantage, etc.)
- [ ] Set up automated data fetching and updating for agents and dashboards
- [ ] Implement API endpoints for real-time news/feeds (RSS parsing, news scraping)

### 📌 **Phase 11: Reporting & Exporting**
- [ ] Implement PDF export functionality (`WeasyPrint`, `html2pdf`)
- [ ] Allow users and agents to generate structured reports & analysis documents

### 📌 **Phase 12: Multi-Agent Collaboration & CrewAI**
- [ ] Set up multi-agent orchestration (CrewAI, AutoGen, LangGraph)
- [ ] Allow collaborative problem-solving between multiple agents
- [ ] Implement complex workflow execution scenarios (agent hierarchies and parallel processing)

### 📌 **Phase 13: DevOps & Deployment**
- [ ] Finalize Docker images and compose files for production environments
- [ ] Establish CI/CD pipeline (Github Actions, Gitlab CI, Jenkins)
- [ ] Create deployment scripts/documentation for various environments (cloud/on-premise)

### 📌 **Phase 14: Advanced Monitoring & Logging**
- [ ] Integrate monitoring and logging systems (Prometheus, Grafana, Logstash, ELK)
- [ ] Develop analytics around agent performance and resource utilization

### 📌 **Phase 15: Security & Compliance**
- [ ] Implement authentication & authorization (JWT, OAuth2)
- [ ] Setup role-based access control (RBAC) for dashboard & agent management
- [ ] Conduct vulnerability scanning and security assessments

### 📌 **Phase 16: Documentation & Tutorials**
- [ ] Create user and developer documentation
- [ ] Build onboarding tutorials and guides for users and developers

